window.PHT_DOCS = {"home":{"lore":"<details open><summary>Comte Cioran's Mausoleum</summary><p>The mausoleum your coterie guarded was for Comte Cioran, an Anarch Brujah who was immensely powerful throughout the twentieth century and ruled Quebec City (and held sway over much of Quebec), keeping independent and holding off all comers, including werewolves, Sabbat, and Camarilla.<br><br>The events leading to his torpor are contradictory, but the guarding of his tomb became a priority for all factions; those who honored his memory wished to prevent a true death or diablerie, and those who feared his return wished to ensure he remained in torpor.<br><br>When he arose, it was with a single-mindedness that led him to the Levant and the rumored location of the Antediluvian founder of the Brujah; leaving the crypt complex a hollow shell.<br><br>Supernature abhors a void, and of late you have been accumulating evidence that this haven now also hosts a wraith or revenant, but you have as yet avoided direct confrontation and have been unable to expel it.</p></details>","tenets":"<p>Chronicle Tenets:<ul><li>Never snitch.</li></ul><ul><li>Respect others, and demand respect.</li></ul><ul><li>Shoot twice, but never shoot first.</li></ul><ul><li>We discipline our own.</li></ul></p>"},"chronicle":[{"slug":"night-of-june-9th-2021","title":"Letters","part":"Wednesday, 9 June 2021","html":"<p>The letters came in Baruch Espinosa's own hand, one to each of them, and none of them said the same thing.</p><p>To Claire:</p><blockquote><p>Our esteemed Warlock</p><p>I believe it will be to your delight that I introduce my latest acquisitions; the seventh, and the ninth that precedes the eighth. Do come and witness my latest acquisition, and sharpen your knives.</p></blockquote><p>To Calliope:</p><blockquote><p>My intemperate Promethea,</p><p>These nights see us poised upon a knife's edge. Our city lacks vision, and is fraught with the squabbles of the leaderless. This detente cannot hold, and when the opportunity arises, power must be grasped, swiftly and without remorse. I care not the face of a new order, for I have seen the rise and fall of Anarch, Camarilla, and Sabbat, each in turn. Use the tool you find most pliant.</p><p>For now, I caution patience. Be ye the virgin with oil for the night, vigilant to seize upon the bridegroom, and to take his place to consummate influence.</p><p>Watchfully yours, Baruch.</p></blockquote><p>To Richart:</p><blockquote><p>My dear ancilla</p><p>In these modern nights, one must assume all discrete communications lack discretion, and that any apparent cryptogram must elicit a remedy, even years hence. As such, and having learned from the failures of past systems, I have found myself enamored with the arts and sciences of steganography. When one reads the surface and is contented, the esoteric meanings may be relayed without danger or harm.</p><p>To this end, may I advise that you watch the fortunes of the Dynamo ARSQ this season, in our city's Chronicle-Telegraph.</p></blockquote><p>To Kamal:</p><blockquote><p>To our austere Assamite,</p><p>A Spaniard ductus walks carelessly through these streets. It would be tragic if the steel trap of a kind of justice were to snap upon him, and he be waylaid.</p><p>His blood is old and strong and, while I am no sommelier, carries certain notes that you may be able to appreciate.</p><p>Yours, Baruch Espinosa</p></blockquote><p>To Nico:</p><blockquote><p>An absent-minded lech such as yourself may notice that histories, both personal and societal, suffer themes and variations. The Levant harkens, leaving a vacuum to be abhorred à la débandade. Surely an oracle such as yourself sees the opportunity in this. It would please me greatly to consult.</p><p>Yours truly, Baruch</p></blockquote><hr><p>They fed first.</p><p>Nico fed from a woman he met out on the town, who had been drinking. Claire took hers from a blood bag at the hospital, which was the kind of thing a night nurse could do. Richart went to the hospital too, and fed from a patient who slept through it. Calliope took someone on the way over.</p><p>Kamal did not feed at all. He arrived on time and well groomed, and his stigmata was showing.</p><hr><p>Nico got there first and hid, to wait for Calliope.</p><p>Richart and Claire arrived together. Richart saw it before they reached the door: the entrance had not been hidden. Baruch always hid the entrance. They went in anyway, and Kamal came in close behind them.</p><p>Richart reached past his ordinary senses into the dark ahead and felt the dead there. Recently dead. He texted the others. Most of them carried burners. Richart carried a smartphone.</p><p>Calliope walked straight up to where Nico was hiding.</p><p>\"You should learn to hide better,\" she said, and they went in together.</p><hr><p>The door to the haven had been broken in with a ram, or something that did a ram's work.</p><p>Inside, the filing cabinets had been tipped over and gone through. Computers and electronics had been ripped out of the walls and taken. And there were two husks on the floor that had been vampires, beheaded and burned.</p><p>Claire went to the files. Baruch had kept information on everybody, most of it banal, and there was a great deal of it, and a great many Kindred named in it. She found full files on Kamal and on Richart. Partial files on Calliope, and on herself. Nothing on Nico.</p><p>Kamal found splattered vitae and tasted it. Two vampires, both older than him: one strong, one a good deal stronger. He could not say whether they were the two on the floor or two others. If one of them was Baruch, it was the weaker.</p><p>Claire looked closer at one of the bodies. Something on its face had melted. It might have been a mask. It might have been Baruch's mask, his signature, out of <em>The Phantom of the Opera</em>.</p><hr><p>Nico wandered off down the hall to the guest room. There had been a struggle there. Blood was thrown across the wall and the floor, and Nico cocked his head and stared into it for some time.</p><p>Kamal came in behind him and tasted this blood too. A third Kindred, and a mortal. The Kindred's blood was the most delicious thing he had ever tasted.</p><p>An argument over artistic differences, Nico decided. Probably.</p><p>Kamal went to find Claire.</p><hr><p>Richart went into the second room. It was open, but nobody had ransacked it. The built-in shelves were full of old things wrapped in newspaper. He took two of the wrapped curios, to find out later what they were.</p><p>Calliope went through the broken door of the last room. A four-poster bed, where Baruch had presumably rested. A wardrobe of suits. A small space for meditation, and somebody had used it recently. She called Kamal in and let him feed from her.</p><p>Claire kept reading. She found a dossier on the Tremere, and took it with her.</p><hr><p>Baruch had been fastidious about his security. If he had died in his own haven, it was a failure of immense proportions.</p><p>Calliope turned to Nico. \"Why don't you have a file?\"</p><p>Nico was as angry about it as she was. He wanted to see what pictures Baruch had kept of him.</p><p>Somebody, or something, had truly killed two powerful vampires in this house, and something had happened to a third. And Baruch had collected far more than any of them had realised.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"night-of-june-10th-2021","title":"The Bank","part":"Thursday, 10 June 2021","html":"<p>Susanna woke in a large room she did not know. There was a one-way mirror on one wall, and cameras. She lay in the dark at its centre, and around her, in a ring, were bright lights.</p><p>She pushed the hunger down and walked out into the light. She called out. She knocked on the door. Nobody came. She went back to the cot in the middle of the room, and then the door opened and two people came in: a man who looked like a priest, and a woman in fatigues who looked like a field medic.</p><hr><p>The others went to Bar le Sacrilège, all but Calliope.</p><p>Fatima was sitting at the bar. Nico's ex. They spoke to the bartender, who told them Faith was in, and busy somewhere else.</p><p>Richart and Nico each knew some of the club, some of the floors below too, though neither of them well. Nico had been seeing things since they left Baruch's. Kamal told them the bodies were buried; he had stayed behind the night before, after the rest of them left, to give the dead their last rites.</p><p>Nico bought a martini and sent it over to Fatima.</p><p>The bartender pointed them to the feeding room. \"Take the left staircase, two floors down.\"</p><p>The first floor down was some kind of kink dungeon. The second had the air of an old west brothel, and a host who came up to them at once. \"It looks like you have need of something.\" He explained that their selection was better than average, though the particular needs of the Ventrue might take some arranging in advance.</p><p>Claire knew one of the faces on offer. Jonah, her thin-blood contact from the hospital. There was also a young Asian woman with pink hair and glasses who read as Kindred. Everyone else there was human.</p><hr><p>The priest-looking man did the talking first.</p><p>\"We know who your companions were, and those blankbodies have been excised from existence. You are condemned, death is the only way out. You have no possibility of being rescued. The only way this will go gently for you is to give up your companions.\"</p><p>\"Are you not a blankbody?\" Susanna said.</p><p>The woman spoke up. \"Your vitals are different from any we've ever seen; it doesn't appear that the infection has fully taken hold. I feel that you're turning into something there is no turning back from, and at that point we would have no choice but to detain you indefinitely, or deal with the infection.\"</p><p>The man in the robe began again. The woman cut him off and steered him out of the room to talk in private. She came back alone, and apologised.</p><p>\"The councillor speaks a little hastily, but your medical records are dubious; a brief examination could assure us as to your risks to national security.\"</p><p>Susanna asked whether she had a choice.</p><p>Asking for her consent, the woman said, was a formality. Strictly speaking, an optional one.</p><p>Susanna asked for time to think about it, and the woman left.</p><hr><p>In the feeding room, Kamal went over to the Kindred woman first, and then to the host, to ask about anything off the menu. Custom orders. Special orders could be placed ahead of time, the host said.</p><p>Nico chose a woman who had had a few drinks, and the two of them went off to a side room.</p><p>When Kamal described what he was after, the host sent him to the VIP lounge: up two flights by the centre stairs, then down two. Speak to Jerome.</p><p>Richart asked the host what that had been about. The clients' preferences were kept discreet. He asked about Faith, and was told she was working, serving the VIP lounge. Richart went after Kamal.</p><hr><p>The woman came back with an offer. They would drop Susanna where they had found her. In exchange, some blood.</p><p>She drew a couple of vials, then walked Susanna through drab, unmarked hallways and out into a garage, where a large van was waiting with half a dozen soldiers to escort her. They drove her to Baruch's and let her out on the street and drove away without a word.</p><p>Her dog came back to her out of the bushes, where it had been hiding.</p><p>Susanna went inside. The door had been battered in and the place turned over, ransacked. The haven was empty.</p><hr><p>Claire went up to Jonah and asked him what he was doing there, and whether there was any bagged blood. Ask at the bar for a juicebox, he said.</p><p>He was sheepish about it. Supplies might be short. A gang had attacked a blood drive and they were dealing with a shortage, and it was causing trouble at the hospital as well. He was on the menu tonight to pay off a boon. He owed the Bank.</p><p>Claire finished the conversation, went up to the bar for a juicebox, and went down to the VIP lounge. Nico followed her once he had fed.</p><hr><p>\"Mr. Giovanni will be the judge of that.\"</p><p>The VIP lounge had been a luxurious room once, and it had been rearranged into something like a throne room.</p><p>Jerome waved Kamal in. \"Come in, come in; Mr. Hussein, am I right? Your reputation precedes you; you've assisted the sheriff in the nascent court, correct? What can I do for you?\"</p><p>Kamal told him. A feeding source that was reliable, ongoing and safe, and in return, his services.</p><p>\"A boon for a boon; that can certainly be arranged.\"</p><p>Jerome set out the terms. Non-lethal feeding at the graveyard near Kamal's haven, in return for Kamal's services on an ongoing basis. No more than twenty-four hours from request to delivery; the same night was possible, but not promised. Richart listened and said nothing.</p><p>As a first payment, Jerome wanted a message carried to the coming Elysium.</p><p>Kamal was taken to a private room for a first feeding, and only sipped.</p><hr><p>Outside, Nico and Claire told Faith about Baruch's haven. She went from distracted to horrified. When they told her Baruch was not in torpor but dead, truly dead, the colour went out of her, and she asked who had done it. She could not see who would. She could not see who even could, not to Baruch. Jerome needed to hear it, she said.</p><p>Nico asked her for a stiff drink first, before he faced Jerome, and she went to get one.</p><p>Kamal went out to feed and came back soon after. Richart joined them outside, and they talked it over.</p><p>Faith came back with Nico's drink. \"0.1 blood alcohol content.\"</p><p>Claire would not go in to see Jerome.</p><p>Nico and Richart went in. Nico bargained first: Fatima banned from the club, in exchange for what they knew. Then they told Jerome what they had seen at Baruch's.</p><p>Jerome stood up suddenly and began to pace. \"When did this happen? This is catastrophic news. Baruch knew everything that happened in this city, from all sides. Was this a Sabbat hit?\"</p><p>They did not know.</p><p>He murmured to himself. \"Jesus Christ... he had some information he was going to present at the Elysium via proxy.\"</p><p>\"I need to call in some favors on the Anarch side; if the Camarilla weren't the perpetrators, then they will be incentivized to find them, as will we; this risks everyone.\"</p><p>To Nico and Richart: \"I'll pay for results. In exchange, if you find a door that needs opening, I'll pull some strings to gain you access in your investigation.\"</p><p>Then he dismissed them. \"If you'll excuse me.\"</p><p>Outside, the four of them worked out what came next. Richart would try to get a message to his sire in the Sabbat, and Nico offered to go with him. Kamal and Claire would go to the sheriff, Javier.</p><hr><p>Richart knew of Sybille, who ran a pack under Milica, and he knew where to find her, or to leave her a message.</p><p>Glaurung had cursed him, once. Richart had escaped, and got enough protection from the Anarchs to stay out of reach of the Sabbat's revenge.</p><p>Sybille had been maybe nineteen when she was turned, and looked fifteen. How old she really was, nobody could say.</p><p>They left the bar before the mortal curfew. In some of these neighbourhoods the Sabbat packs enforced the curfew, and enforced it hard.</p><p>They came to the back entrance of Sybille's ritual space from the alley. There was a ward on the door, an alarm. Richart pushed through it.</p><p>Sybille was surrounded by books, and whiteboards, all in disarray. She turned on them angrily. \"Roscoe, I told you to stop... who are you?\"</p><p>Then: \"Oh, Richart; what the hell are you doing here?\"</p><p>And then: \"Thank you, but that won't save you.\"</p><p>And then: \"Now you have me intrigued. Whose murder are we talking about?\"</p><p>\"The blessed one,\" Nico said.</p><p>\"There was no love lost but Baruch was an asset nonetheless. We try not to throw assets away needlessly. Are you accusing us of this?\"</p><p>Nico had admired Sybille's boots once before. He asked about Milica's.</p><p>\"Milica has exquisite boots. What do you want of her?\"</p><p>She agreed to pass the message on. \"I can see Jerome using this as a pretext for all sorts of trouble.\" And: \"Can you give me the location of the blessed one's haven?\"</p><p>Afterwards they went to the mausoleum.</p><hr><p>Kamal and Claire got a ride out to Javier's haven in Sainte-Foy.</p><p>Javier had been aloof in the past and turned down attempts to work with him, but he got along well enough with Kamal. He let them in. He had been working through the security for the coming Elysium.</p><p>They told him what they had found at Baruch's. The Camarilla claimed jurisdiction, Javier admitted, but had no real authority there, and Baruch had formally been Anarch. Still, he asked them to take him to the scene. He drove.</p><hr><p>On the way in, Kamal saw that someone had disturbed the entrance since he left.</p><p>They went in carefully, and found Susanna there with her dog, looking around, lost. When she turned, Claire caught a glimpse of a third eye in her forehead.</p><p>Her clothes were scuffed and torn. Whatever injuries had gone with them had already healed.</p><p>Javier suggested it, and Kamal and Claire offered to take Susanna back to the coterie's haven.</p><p>Kamal wanted to match her to the blood on the guest-room walls, and asked for a sample. She hesitated, and looked into him. His aura told her he was Kindred like her, that he meant her no harm, and that he believed he had the authority to ask.</p><p>Claire unpacked her equipment and drew a vial of Susanna's blood. She handed it to Kamal. He tasted it. He dabbed again. Then he drained the vial and went into a hunger frenzy.</p><p>It was the blood from the guest room, no question. Javier had to hold him back bodily to keep him off Susanna.</p><p>Claire tried to thicken her own blood, and could not. She gave Kamal her wrist anyway, enough to start bringing him down, and then took it back. Kamal lunged for more. Javier stopped him.</p><p>Susanna had frenzied herself, though in more controlled circumstances, and knew what she was watching.</p><p>She offered a little more. Claire drew a second vial and this time tasted it herself instead of giving it to Kamal. She felt the frenzy pull at her and held against it, and she was certain: Susanna was the third Kindred.</p><p>Kamal was mortified by what he had done. He was in awe of Claire.</p><p>They questioned Susanna, and learned that she and her sire, Estelle, were to have been introduced to the Camarilla by Baruch at the next Elysium.</p><p>Javier looked the room over. He ripped a camera out of the wall and crushed it. Then he went over the other walls, and found two more.</p><p>\"I don't know whose these are, but I don't appreciate being watched by parties unknown.\"</p><p>He would go over the scene himself, he said, and asked them to go on ahead and take Susanna with them.</p><p>Susanna told them how she had been taken and let go. Now she remembered: the soldiers wore CSIS patches. She had not been blindfolded, but she could not see out of the van, and she did not know the way they had come.</p><hr><p>Claire and Kamal brought Susanna to the mausoleum, where Richart, Nico and Calliope were waiting. Calliope had come back with a freezer box of bagged blood.</p><p>They made their introductions. It was getting on for dawn.</p><p>As the day's sleep came down on them, something howled out of the earth beneath their feet.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"night-of-june-11th-2021","title":"The Wight","part":"Friday, 11 June 2021","html":"<p>Susanna woke in a hunger frenzy.</p><p>The rest of them woke to find Calliope squared off against a wight. It had come up out of the soil, roaring, and it went for her. They fought it, and it tore into Calliope and put her down, into torpor.</p><p>This was the haunting, then, the presence they had been feeling in the crypt, given a body. Richart was sure it was alone. Perhaps it had lain latent until now, or in torpor.</p><p>Nico was entirely calm about it, and tried to reason with it. Kamal called up his blood. Claire readied hers. The wight turned on Richart and went for him.</p><p>Susanna steered herself at it. She threw herself onto its back and sank her teeth into its neck, and drank, and the hunger eased, and the frenzy let go of her.</p><p>Nico told it to be still, and it was.</p><p>Kamal reached into it and choked the blood in its body, and still it fought, and fought hard.</p><p>Richart drew his handgun and fired. The bullets buried themselves in its flesh.</p><p>The wight went for Claire. She tried to pull away, and it came down on her, and her leg bent in a direction legs do not go.</p><p>Nico was disappointed that it had not listened. \"Sit!\"</p><p>Kamal jumped on it and latched on to feed as well. The body went slack and sank into torpor.</p><hr><p>Richart looked at Claire. He took her knife and cut the leg of her trousers away, and his tongue reached out to the leg, and under it the flesh moved and set into a shape that would carry her weight again.</p><p>\"So what exactly was that?\" Richart said.</p><p>\"Our bashful friend finally made an appearance,\" said Nico.</p><p>\"It came from the earth,\" said Richart. \"A distinctly Tzimisce approach, if I do say so.\"</p><p>Kamal could tell it was a strong vampire, though not as strong as the one who had lain here under guard. Either it had only just come out of torpor, or it had been hiding a long time.</p><p>Claire tasted its blood. It was what she had been warned of: what a Kindred becomes when the Beast takes them wholly. It would be out for about a month.</p><hr><p>They caught each other up. Susanna was introduced to Richart and Nico. She belonged to no faction, she said. Mortals had taken her, and then let her go. She believed she had kept her third eye hidden from them, but she had had to give them some of her blood.</p><p>Claire spoke up. She thought Susanna's blood was powerful. That she might be an asset, or else someone in need of protecting.</p><p>\"How do you feel about boots?\" Nico asked her.</p><p>\"The more boots, the better.\"</p><p>\"A useful asset.\"</p><p>\"She was first after Calli to jump into the scrap, as well,\" said Richart.</p><p>Richart told them he had passed the news of the attack on Baruch's to his contacts. Nico began researching fashion for Elysium. Kamal thought the eyes Nico had been seeing might have been the cameras Javier found in Baruch's haven.</p><p>Richart looked the wight's body over. He fetched a stake he had hidden away for just this kind of emergency, and staked it, to be safe.</p><p>Kamal went to feed Calliope some of his own vitae to help her wake. Richart stopped him, and had Nico do it instead. It would take her a couple of nights to come fully back.</p><p>Claire noticed that the bags of blood Calliope had brought had been meant for the hospital.</p><hr><p>Nico had a vision. Susanna, lying in the dark, a glow all around her, looking up, and above her the northern lights. Watchers stood all around: some dressed as priests, some in fatigues, some in suits. One of the men wore the regalia of the Society of St. Leopold, which went back to the first Inquisition.</p><p>\"The eyes have arms and badges!\" Nico screamed, staring at nothing on the wall, stroking it.</p><p>Richart asked Susanna whether he might reach into her memory and try to bring back anything she had lost. He tried. There was nothing there to bring back.</p><hr><p>Kamal wanted to walk Susanna's blood, to learn whether she carried any bonds. He laid out the risks, frenzy above all. Claire, Richart and Kamal began to talk through how it would be done, and Susanna broke in, confused.</p><p>To earn their trust, she told them. She was Salubri. Estelle had been her sire. She was willing to give a little more blood, safely, if it would help untangle what had happened.</p><p>Claire was surprised. It was nothing like what the Tremere had taught her about the Salubri. She said nothing.</p><p>Nico was still hallucinating at the walls. Susanna asked him about his boots, and whether he had a special pair for the event. That got his attention. He described a pair of asymmetrical boots, and then went back to walking in circles inside his vision. Richart gave him three hundred dollars to buy a pair of cufflinks fit for Elysium.</p><hr><p>Kamal and Richart went off by themselves to do it. First Richart sat Kamal down and put his rotting hands on Kamal's shoulders, and his tongue ran down Kamal's neck and up to his ear, and under it he took some of the quickness out of Kamal's body and gave it to his will.</p><p>Claire had drawn more of Susanna's blood. She brought it to Kamal with a chalice.</p><p>Kamal drank. He braced against the frenzy, and this time he beat it, and beat it for good: her blood would not have that hold on him again.</p><p>The walk began. He felt an older Kindred, Tzimisce, close and recent. And another thing bound to Susanna, but further off.</p><p>When it was done he called Susanna in, and Richart came too. Kamal told her what he had seen.</p><p>\"One regnant, and one thrall.\"</p><p>Susanna knew nothing of either bond.</p><hr><p>Outside the mausoleum, someone had left a sealed packet for Richart in a dead drop, and a note with it. He had an invitation. He was to attend the Elysium the following night.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"night-of-june-12th-2021","title":"Elysium","part":"Saturday, 12 June 2021","html":"<p>The next night Richart healed, and Claire's leg mended a little more. The changes Richart had worked on Kamal came undone.</p><p>On the way, Kamal described what the blood walk had shown him: the Kindred that Susanna was bound to. Richart knew that description. He suspected it was Glaurung, bishop of the Sabbat.</p><p>Richart mentioned that he was delivering a package. Kamal asked what was in it. They thought about opening it without anyone knowing, and in the end left it as it was.</p><p>Nico produced the cufflinks: silver rectangles with an emerald at the centre. Richart wore a four-screen shirt, a dark grey tie and a fitted charcoal suit. He looked dapper, and far too young. The two of them looked like frat boys who had cleaned up nice.</p><hr><p>Anselm, masked, announced each Kindred as they came into Elysium. Ghouls in beautiful clothes walked the room with tall, thin, lidded glasses of blood.</p><p>Richart and Kamal arrived together. Nico was there already and enjoying himself. Claire took Susanna to her chantry instead.</p><p>The Toreador had style, and Mohamed had outdone himself. Nico was talking to Maggie, who was urging him to think about joining the Tower.</p><p>Kamal wore a suit and a bow tie. He saw Javier off to one side, his hair tied up in a bun. Prince Beatrice stood at the room's natural centre, talking with Gisele and others. The formal part of the night had not yet begun.</p><p>Richart found Mohamed and asked that the delivery of his package be put on the agenda. Mohamed assured him that he was under Elysium's protection, and reminded him, distrustfully, of what the Masquerade required. Kamal joined them and asked for a guest list. Mohamed said he would get him one, though he had given one to Javier already. Was there a security concern? There was not, Kamal said.</p><hr><p>In the chantry, Claire showed Susanna around and told her something of her work. What she had learned about the Salubri was very different, she said. That they had been all but wiped out. She was curious about Susanna's lineage, and about blood as potent as hers.</p><p>\"The blood potency is definitely part of the reason we have been hunted,\" said Susanna. \"I'll choose to trust you, and acknowledge that there has been animosity between our clans.\"</p><p>\"We were told that you participated in a kind of verboten diablerie,\" said Claire. \"You were boogiemen, and there wasn't much discussion of success with Golconda. But I think you should be protected, which is why I didn't bring us to the Elysium, yet.\"</p><hr><p>The formal part of the Elysium began, and Javier opened it.</p><p>He described the destruction of an Anarch haven and of two unaffiliated Kindred, most likely by the Sabbat, an escalation of pointless conflict that put the Masquerade at risk. It drove home how badly the Camarilla needed to extend its reach and secure Quebec City against that kind of reckless gamble. He described the scene, the reckless use of technology. It was part clinical report, part polemic, part speculation.</p><p>He called Kamal forward to corroborate. Kamal thanked him, said he had nothing to add, and stepped down. Gisele thanked Javier.</p><p>Gisele called Richart forward. He brought the package. Prince Beatrice took it, thanked him, and opened it: a book, and a sheaf of papers. She handed the book to Gisele and read the papers, and then she answered him.</p><p>\"Thank you, and do enjoy the rest of the night, but understand that this invitation will not recur.\"</p><p>Richart bowed his head. \"It was not my decision.\"</p><p>\"We welcome the unaffiliated,\" Anselm announced, \"Jerome Giovanni.\"</p><p>Jerome was already strolling in as he said it, confident, straight for the Prince. Richart moved back towards an exit.</p><hr><p>Claire gave Susanna a discreet sash to cover her forehead, and they came to the Elysium late, just after Jerome. Claire talked Anselm out of announcing them; she did not want to disturb the proceedings.</p><p>She watched Jerome walk up to the Prince, and then swerve off to berate Michel instead: about his childe, and a delinquent payment that was now Michel's responsibility. Michel was blindsided. He told Jerome he was surely mistaken.</p><p>Kamal and Nico saw Claire and Susanna come in. Richart was listening to Jerome and Michel.</p><p>Kamal went back to Javier. They should not be so certain it was the Sabbat, he said. He believed mortals had been involved.</p><p>He felt Javier's will press into his mind. \"We are certain of the Sabbat's disruptive influence.\"</p><p>Kamal understood. Blaming the Sabbat was politically convenient, whether or not the Sabbat had done it, and the Anarchs were unlikely to stand in the way. As he walked off, Mohamed handed him a folder. It had not been checked against who was actually there.</p><p>Susanna opened her senses to the room. The space was warded, and the waiting staff were all ghouls. She picked out Nico, Kamal and Richart in the crowd.</p><p>\"Wow, this is quite the affair,\" she said. \"Is this pretty typical?\"</p><p>Claire was panicking. She tried to answer calmly while she kept out of Jerome's line of sight.</p><hr><p>Michel's eyes found Claire, and he came straight for her. She ducked into a side room. He caught up with her there.</p><p>\"Is that why you tried to stand us up? What foolishness have you gotten us into?\"</p><p>\"I felt like it was a solid plan, and it fizzled, but I'm working on something that will make good on everything.\"</p><p>\"Your 'plans' involved standing up and withholding payment on a major boon to a kindred you should never have owed in the first place. Why did you not simply ask? We could have coordinated something, whatever it was.\"</p><p>\"Well, it was going to be a surprise, an awesome thing, but I promise I'll get it handled.\"</p><p>\"Give me one good reason why I shouldn't hand you over to Jerome right now.\"</p><p>Claire took out the vial of Susanna's blood.</p><p>\"What's that?\"</p><p>She put a drop on her finger and held it out to him. Michel did not understand. He licked it anyway, and his eyes lit up.</p><p>\"Is.... is that what I think it is?\"</p><p>\"Yes, I don't know how it exists here, but...\"</p><p>\"But there's more where that came from?\"</p><p>\"...yes.\"</p><p>\"Don't speak to Jerome of this. Let me talk to the Prince. We can find a way to get him off your back. Give me ten minutes and I'll have Jerome removed from the Elysium. I don't know how you managed to obtain that, but it's a coup.\"</p><p>Claire sighed, and slumped against the wall.</p><hr><p>Kamal went through the papers. Glaurung was not on the list. Jerome was. So were Baruch and Estelle, both struck out.</p><p>Susanna saw Estelle's name and asked Kamal about it, and about the wards. Kamal knew them: wards against ghouls and spirits.</p><p>\"Was that what Nico was referring to?\"</p><p>\"We're never quite sure what Nico is referring to.\"</p><hr><p>Nico noticed a ghoul standing a little apart from the Prince, and it looked like one of the figures from his vision. He went over and said hello.</p><p>\"Were you in my vision?\"</p><p>\"Well, I see you now.\"</p><p>\"Not my vision now, earlier, with the walls and the eyes.\"</p><p>\"I don't know.\"</p><p>\"Could you call the Prince over here?\"</p><p>\"She seems occupied.\"</p><p>\"Make an attempt.\"</p><p>The ghoul went and spoke to the Prince, and when she had finished with the petition in front of her, she came over.</p><p>\"Thank you for coming,\" said Beatrice. \"Are you considering joining our endeavor?\"</p><p>\"I'm not much of a joiner. I have a question for you; have you had any news of the northern lights, moving?\"</p><p>\"...yes. A true Aurora.\"</p><p>\"Yes! With many eyes and many arms. And sometimes badges. This is an endeavor we should all be part of.\"</p><p>\"It's an endeavor that is a sign of power for some, doom for others.\"</p><p>\"Agreed. I have friends here, they could be helpful, we are concerned that the doom might reach too many of us.\"</p><p>\"Too many is subjective.\"</p><p>\"You don't enjoy kindred? They're a good time! You don't want the doom to reach all of us.\"</p><p>\"I'm confident that those of the Camarilla will be spared.\"</p><p>\"Then perhaps you underestimate the Aurora; it is a true Aurora.\"</p><p>\"Let's remain in touch,\" said the Prince, \"but the offer of protection is only for joiners; simply being a guest at Elysium is insufficient. Good evening.\"</p><hr><p>Richart saw Michel storm into the room, take Jerome by the elbow, and walk him out of it.</p><p>He went over to Kamal and Susanna and asked where Claire was. Coming here had been a terrible idea, he said, and he did not think much of Claire for deciding it.</p><p>Gisele came up. \"The Prince has a response for you, could you join us?\"</p><p>The Prince came over. \"We have drafted a brief but hopefully sufficient response.\" She gave him an unsealed package, a small wooden box about the size of a novel, and asked him to deliver it to Milica and Glaurung.</p><p>Richart went to Nico. \"I think it's in everyone's best interests to leave with Susanna; could you manage a distraction?\"</p><p>Nico could. Richart went to get the others ready. Claire came back in from the other side of the room and joined them.</p><p>Nico started drinking loudly and trying to get everyone around him to join in. Then he dropped his glass and began screaming about arms reaching down out of the ceiling. Javier came over and held him down. It was distraction enough, and the others got out.</p><p>Susanna left reluctantly. She asked Claire whether they could go back to the chantry, but in the end they went back to the mausoleum. There was safety in numbers.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"night-of-june-13th-2021","title":"Follow the Boots","part":"Sunday, 13 June 2021","html":"<p>Susanna woke to find one of Baruch's dossiers waiting for her, with a note from Richart. She opened it and read.</p><p>Baruch had been shopping her and Estelle to all three factions. A bidding war, of a kind: the most safety for them, the biggest cut for him, in boons and in intelligence. Glaurung had been his contact for the Sabbat. Gisele for the Camarilla. Jerome for the Anarchs.</p><p>Claire fed from one of the blood bags, and then looked at Susanna with interest.</p><hr><p>Nico wanted them to come on a vision journey with him. He went out alone to feed first.</p><p>They met at Bar le Sacrilège and took a private room. Nico and Susanna went under together. Claire stood watch.</p><p>Nico's vision was a strong one, and it was about AURORA. They had been working from Camarilla intelligence, and it had come from Gisele Singh, the seneschal.</p><p>He came out of it in a panic. \"Get your hands off me, hands off me.\"</p><p>\"That was disturbing,\" Susanna said. \"Nico, it wasn't real.\"</p><p>Claire had frozen, not knowing what to do.</p><p>When he had calmed down, Nico said, \"We need to reach out to our friends, they're in Sabbat territory.\"</p><p>Did he have a contact, Claire asked, or a lead?</p><p>\"We need to follow the boots.\"</p><hr><p>They decided to go back to the mausoleum and take the wight to the Sabbat, as a peace offering.</p><p>They commandeered an Uber and loaded the staked wight into the back, and Nico directed the driver to the alley behind Sybille's haven. He went in first, and left the carrying of the wight to Claire and Susanna, who struggled in after him.</p><p>Nico introduced Claire and Susanna as his friends, and the wight as his dog.</p><p>Claire realised where she was, and went pale. She introduced herself civilly, and hoped nobody knew who she was.</p><p>Nico left the wight with Sybille. He would train it with her, he said; it was not simply hers to do anything she liked with. Claire excused herself, took Susanna, and went back to the mausoleum.</p><p>Not long after they left, the Spaniard arrived. Nico asked him about AURORA, and the Spaniard hatched a plan. A gift of coordinates, from the Sabbat bishops to the Camarilla, for the Camarilla to pass to AURORA. But Nico was to swap them for the coordinates of the Prince's haven, and set the court and AURORA on each other.</p><p>Nico went back to the mausoleum.</p><hr><p>Back at the haven, Claire confessed. She had given away the secret of Susanna's blood to a superior whose intentions were hard to read and rarely kind. She did not know how to protect Susanna now, and she had put her in more danger. She was sorry.</p><p>Susanna was crushed. Claire suggested they find a way to turn it aside.</p><p>Nico came in. He complimented Susanna's thigh-high purple sparkly boots, and told them the mustache had told him to tell the Prince where to go.</p><p>Claire was worried, and more so when she learned it had been a Sabbat mustache. In the end she agreed to take the coordinates to Gisele. Nico would stay with Susanna. He gave Claire one of his two pieces of paper, and did not check which set of coordinates it was.</p><hr><p>While Claire was gone, Nico found something to feed Sunshine, and Susanna went to talk to Jerome. Nico went with her.</p><p>Susanna told Jerome she knew he and Baruch had been discussing particulars. In the end they agreed: Susanna would have a home under the protection of the Gangrel, the Quebecois Anarch motorcycle gang, in exchange for a major boon. Matthieu would be told to find her at the mausoleum.</p><hr><p>Claire met Gisele. The paper, she explained, was information about where the Sabbat would be, a meeting perhaps, and it had come by way of Nico. She suggested Gisele ask the Prince for the context. Gisele thanked her, and dismissed her.</p><p>A text went to a number Gisele was known to watch.</p><p><em>There is a trap for the Camarilla at the set of coordinates that Nico possesses, not the ones Claire passed to the Prince.</em></p><hr><p>Nico, Claire and Susanna went out to a club. They persuaded the bouncer that Sunshine was a cat, and allowed on the premises, and not a dog.</p><p>Nico offered Susanna the mausoleum as a home, so the \"cat\" could stay. It could play with the \"dog\", he said, the wight, once he had it trained.</p><p>They went over what Nico and Susanna had each seen in the vision. Tendrils across the city. Nerve clusters. There had been two of those, and Claire recognised one of them: a warehouse that matched Susanna's description of the place where she had been held.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"night-of-june-14th-2021","title":"The Fairmont","part":"Monday, 14 June 2021","html":"<p>Nico, Claire and Susanna woke to find Calliope still in torpor, and Richart and Kamal gone.</p><p>Claire took Susanna aside to talk in private. She proposed an alliance, just the two of them. If Susanna would give her vitae, there was a ritual Claire had been learning that could overwhelm any enemy or threat. She admitted she had never quite managed it before. Susanna's blood, she believed, would make the difference.</p><p>Susanna wanted to hold off on any arrangement until Jerome's contact arrived. Claire was shocked. Susanna had already made a deal with Jerome.</p><p>Jerome could not be trusted, Nico said. He poured weak drinks.</p><hr><p>Matthieu arrived with several other bikers, to collect Susanna as promised. She asked for a little time. Matthieu left one of his bikers outside to bring her along when she was ready.</p><p>He asked whether they had seen Calliope. She owed him for some bagged blood. She was in torpor, they told him. He took the blood back, and left. Claire's eyes followed the cooler out of the door.</p><p>Nico asked Susanna what she had offered Jerome.</p><p>\"A major boon,\" she said. For a safe haven.</p><p>Nico turned to Claire. \"We should get her to stay.\"</p><p>\"I'm confused,\" said Susanna. \"Why would I need to stay to be protected?\"</p><p>Claire's answer confused her more. But Claire talked her into staying with them a little while, and into giving some blood so Claire could attempt the ritual.</p><p>Susanna wanted a rider on it, a magical one: if either of them betrayed the other, they would be struck down into torpor. Claire agreed in principle. She did not know how to do such a thing. Michel might. A blood bond might serve, but that Claire could not do.</p><hr><p>There was a disturbance outside. Javier and Michel came in.</p><p>Claire looked surprised. \"What do you need?\"</p><p>Michel looked around the room. \"By process of elimination, I take it she's the one?\"</p><p>Claire tried to lie, and it went terribly. Michel glared at her. What kind of stunt was she trying to pull?</p><p>\"I'm here because of the attempted Sabbat ambush. How did they get those coordinates? The ones you gave me were for Beatrice's haven.\"</p><p>Claire pointed at Nico.</p><p>\"How do they know where the Prince sleeps?\"</p><p>Nico shrugged.</p><p>\"Well, you're going to help us hit them back.\"</p><p>\"That doesn't sound like fun, no thanks.\"</p><p>Michel bared his teeth. \"I wasn't asking.\"</p><p>Kamal came back in. \"We know where AURORA is going to hit next, we need to help move them move out.\"</p><p>Kamal, Michel and Javier went out.</p><hr><p>Claire slumped. \"He knows who you are now, Susanna, and Michel is dangerous.\"</p><p>Nico bought them some time. He hung a sock on the outside doorknob and locked the door from the inside.</p><p>Claire spent an hour preparing the ritual, with Susanna's blood mixed into the bagged blood, and worked it on herself. Susanna said she trusted her.</p><p>Then Susanna understood what she had agreed to. For now, she depended entirely on Claire for her protection, and that upset her.</p><p>Susanna left first, with the Gangrel biker, for Matthieu's haven.</p><hr><p>Claire and Nico went out after her. Kamal told them she had gone, and took them to the Fairmont, where Nico's coordinates led. He brought them in by a side entrance, and they moved through it quietly.</p><p>In a room off the corridor, Gisele, Javier and Michel were watching security camera footage. On the screens were Glaurung and several other Sabbat, at least, armed.</p><p>\"Come in,\" said Javier, \"action is about to start.\"</p><p>Michel turned to Claire. \"Where is she?\"</p><p>\"Maybe another time? I didn't want to ruin this moment.\"</p><p>\"No. Where is she?\"</p><p>\"Jerome. She made a deal with Jerome.\"</p><p>Michel was stunned, and then he lashed out. \"You gave the Salubri to the Anarchs?\"</p><p>\"She sort of ran off. We...\"</p><p>\"You let her run away?\"</p><p>\"She's her own person, man,\" said Nico.</p><p>\"No, she is a tool, and she's ours to be wielded.\"</p><p>\"If she were, she would be here.\"</p><p>\"If my childer were competent, that would be true.\"</p><p>\"Sounds like you're a bad parent,\" Nico said.</p><p>\"We'll deal with you after.\"</p><hr><p>On the screens, the lights went out. Beams of light swung around in the dark, soldiers coming in, muzzle flashes, and it was hard to tell what was happening. They could hear that it was happening just down the hall.</p><p>Javier stood. \"Let's ensure no one gets out.\"</p><p>He and Kamal ran down the hallway. Claire stayed back with Nico.</p><p>\"Do you want me to go retrieve her now?\" she asked Michel.</p><p>\"We need to decapitate the Sabbat while we can, but afterwards I need you to chase her down. We cannot allow a prize like that to get away.\"</p><p>Claire went down the hall.</p><p>A couple of soldiers burst out of the room ahead, terrified, and ran. Behind them came a roar, and the wight, and it ran them down and tore them limb from limb. Nico heard the roar and jumped up and ran after it. Kamal and Claire took the chance and slipped into the room.</p><hr><p>The room was wrecked, and the stench of blood was thick. There were figures in the shadows all around them. Claire caught sight of Sybille at the edge of her vision and wished she had not come. She froze. Then she screamed and began to back away, and backed into someone.</p><p>Two hands took hold of her shoulders. She turned, and it was Richart, and she breathed out.</p><p>The hands were real, though. Not rotting any more. Not sewn on.</p><p>\"What's going on Richart?\"</p><p>Richart grinned. \"The Camarilla thought we had set a trap for them, but we knew they would send their human agents in their stead. Do you realize the trouble your friends have been causing, in breach of their beloved masquerade?\"</p><p>Claire pushed back. \"You've been using AURORA to target havens across the city; Baruch?\"</p><p>\"It wasn't the Sabbat. Why would we stoop to using a vessel like that?\"</p><p>Kamal and Javier had seen how badly outnumbered they were, and were giving themselves up to the Tzimisce, who shaped restraints for them out of flesh.</p><hr><p>Down the hall, Nico caught up with the wight. It was chewing on a soldier.</p><p>\"Good doggy! Good doggy!\"</p><p>He picked up a severed arm and threw it back down the hall, and tried to get it to fetch.</p><hr><p>\"Were you aware of any of this?\" Claire asked Kamal.</p><p>Kamal turned to Javier. \"It seems we were told what we needed for our own protection.\"</p><p>Claire asked Richart how he could betray his coterie. The Sabbat had given him back his hands, he said, and a position of authority.</p><p>Claire's arms caught fire.</p><p>Sybille hissed at the flames and drew back, and Richart backed away. Claire raised both arms, and Milica was gibbering with terror. Kamal kept his eyes carefully down. Glaurung was wary. Javier was on the floor, convulsing.</p><p>Claire tried to get Kamal to help her. He showed her his hands, bound in flesh, and asked her to cover him while he ran for help.</p><hr><p>The wight came back with the arm. \"Good doggy,\" Nico said, and held it with his eyes, and then the screaming started in the room and he saw Kamal come out. Nico and the wight followed Kamal back to Michel and Gisele.</p><p>\"We need to help Claire and Javier,\" said Kamal, \"the Sabbat have them!\"</p><p>Gisele and Michel argued that they should get out now, and come back with reinforcements.</p><p>Nico told the wight to attack Michel. It did not do much damage. It got Michel's attention, though, when Nico called it back to heel.</p><p>\"That thing's yours?\"</p><p>\"It is. We have things to do. Will you play nicely?\"</p><p>\"We need to get out.\"</p><p>\"We have folks to help. Be useful.\"</p><p>Michel looked at him. \"Be my guest.\"</p><hr><p>Claire saw that Glaurung had a gun on her. She dove for his ankles with her arms ablaze. Both of them missed: he fired as he jumped back.</p><p>Nico arrived. \"Need anything?\"</p><p>\"Thank god,\" said Claire, and pointed at Glaurung.</p><p>Glaurung glared at Nico. \"Get her out of here, she's insane.\"</p><p>He fired at Claire again, and this time he hit her. Nico set the wight on him. When the gun went flying, Nico called it off.</p><p>\"What are your intentions here?\" Glaurung asked him.</p><p>\"What would you like to do next, Claire?\"</p><p>Claire had got up and backed away to Nico's side. \"We need to get out of here, we need to get Javier up.\"</p><p>\"We need to deal with them decisively,\" said Kamal. \"We cannot allow a rot like this to fester.\"</p><p>Nico had the wight pick Javier up. Then he spoke to all of the Sabbat. \"If we let you go, I need a favor.\"</p><p>Richart chided him. \"They won't owe you anything if they allow you to leave without the final death. If Claire and Kamal want to be idiots that's on them, not you.\"</p><p>Nico pointed at Claire's arms. \"You see those? If we leave, they owe us.\"</p><p>Richart looked at Milica, and back, and nodded.</p><p>\"Fine,\" said Glaurung. \"If you all leave.\"</p><p>Claire looked at Kamal, doubtful, and backed out through the door. Kamal went last, resigned, once it was clear neither of his allies was staying.</p>","written":true},{"slug":"epilogue","title":"Epilogue","part":"The nights that followed","html":"<p>What Jerome had offered Susanna turned out to be real. The major boon still hung over her. But night to night, life with the Gangrel was amiable, and they defended their territory hard. There were rumours of other beasts in the woods nearby. So far, nothing had come out of them.</p><hr><p>Nico became a major Anarch player, all the more because he had connections and could deal directly with the Sabbat and with the Camarilla both. He got a name as a dealbroker. He was very curious about AURORA, which had gone quiet. The attack at the Fairmont had cost them, and drawn the Sabbat's attention. Nico watched them, and made sure what they did stayed inside the bounds he thought acceptable.</p><hr><p>Claire was in a delicate position. She had walked away from the mess with the Sabbat, but the Sabbat had not been dealt with, and Kamal was upset about it. And she had failed to bring Susanna back, which made her place with Michel and the Camarilla delicate too.</p><p>She reached out to Susanna, and tried to tempt her with knowledge, with blood sorcery. But Claire still worked under Michel, and so whatever passed between them, and whatever trust, went only so far.</p><p>She had worked the ritual, and worked it in a way that until then had only been a theory. That raised her in Michel's esteem. It also made him press her harder to bring Susanna in.</p><hr><p>Richart was satisfied with how it had ended. He was thankful it had not come, in the end, to extermination.</p><hr><p>Kamal was stuck. The big push for a Camarilla takeover had had to wait, and so he waited. He still resented Claire, a little, for shrinking back when it mattered.</p>","written":true}],"letters":"<details open><summary>Tremere</summary><p>Our esteemed Warlock</p><p>I believe it will be to your delight that I introduce my latest acquisitions; the seventh, and the ninth that precedes the eighth. Do come and witness my latest acquisition, and sharpen your knives.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/e0a91a6ad8862d23.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/e0a91a6ad8862d23.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></details><details open><summary>Brujah</summary><p>My intemperate Promethea,</p><p>These nights see us poised upon a knife's edge. Our city lacks vision, and is fraught with the squabbles of the leaderless. This detente cannot hold, and when the opportunity arises, power must be grasped, swiftly and without remorse. I care not the face of a new order, for I have seen the rise and fall of Anarch, Camarilla, and Sabbat, each in turn. Use the tool you find most pliant.</p><p>For now, I caution patience. Be ye the virgin with oil for the night, vigilant to seize upon the bridegroom, and to take his place to consummate influence.</p><p>Watchfully yours, Baruch.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/caf637c07e819dca.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/caf637c07e819dca.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></details><details open><summary>Tzimisce</summary><p>My dear ancilla</p><p>In these modern nights, one must assume all discrete communications lack discretion, and that any apparent cryptogram must elicit a remedy, even years hence. As such, and having learned from the failures of past systems, I have found myself enamored with the arts and sciences of steganography. When one reads the surface and is contented, the esoteric meanings may be relayed without danger or harm.</p><p>To this end, may I advise that you watch the fortunes of the Dynamo ARSQ this season, in our city's Chronicle-Telegraph.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/f24f6cc6aeaefe37.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/f24f6cc6aeaefe37.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure></details><details open><summary>Banu Haqim</summary><p>To our austere Assamite,</p><p>A Spaniard ductus walks carelessly through these streets. It would be tragic if the steel trap of a kind of justice were to snap upon him, and he be waylaid.</p><p>His blood is old and strong and, while I am no sommelier, carries certain notes that you may be able to appreciate.</p><p>Yours, Baruch Espinosa</p></details><details open><summary>Malkavian</summary><p>An absent-minded lech such as yourself may notice that histories, both personal and societal, suffer themes and variations. The Levant harkens, leaving a vacuum to be abhorred à la débandade. Surely an oracle such as yourself sees the opportunity in this. It would please me greatly to consult.</p><p>Yours truly, Baruch</p></details><details open><summary>Salubri</summary></details>","coterie":[{"slug":"claire-breguet","name":"Claire Breguet","clan":"Tremere","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Fledgling (13th Generation)","concept":"Night Nurse, House Tremere","bloodPotency":"1","humanity":"7","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/claire-breguet.webp","html":"<h3>To-Do</h3><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Drug addiction?</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Claire has sensitive teeth/fangs, prone to brain freezes.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> She loves scrubs. Thinks they're the ultimate kind of clothing.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Always needs to know the time; very regimented</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Ambition &amp; Desire</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> 1-2 more convictions and touchstones</li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/e0a91a6ad8862d23.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/e0a91a6ad8862d23.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h3>Character Notes</h3><h3>History</h3><h3>Ambition</h3><p>Rebuilding the Pyramid, with House Tremere in charge.</p><h3>Desire</h3><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><h3>Lore Notes</h3><p>In 2008, a united USSOCOM and Vatican ESOG force augmented with experienced Brazilian hunter-killer teams stormed the Vienna Chantry of Clan Tremere and destroyed it, blaming it to an ISIS terror attack to the public.</p><details open><summary>Rituals</summary><p><strong>Level 1 Rituals:</strong><p><strong>Blood Walk</strong>: An advanced version of <strong>A Taste for Blood</strong>, the caster is able to learn even more information about another Kindred from their vitae.</p><p><strong>Bloody Message:</strong> This ritual allows the vampire to write a message in blood, unto a piece of paper, that will vanish once the recipient reads it.</p><p><strong>Clinging of the Insect</strong>: Gives the caster the ability to cling to walls like a spider.</p><p><strong>Coax the Garden</strong>: Allows the caster to manipulate plant life, to their defense.</p><p><strong>Craft Bloodstone</strong>: Creates a Bloodstone, a magical tracking device.</p><p><strong>Dampen the Fear</strong>: Temporarily subdues the caster's fear of fire.</p><p><strong>Herd Ward:</strong> This rituals allows the vampire to protect their herd, from poachers.</p><p><strong>Letter Ward:</strong> This ritual is used by Tremere, when they want to make sure the missives they send are protected.</p><p><strong>Unseen Underground</strong>: Turns the caster invisible for a time, when they are underground.</p><p><strong>Wake with Evening's Freshness</strong>: Allows the caster to freshly awaken from torpor during the day as if it were already evening.</p><p><strong>Ward Against Ghouls</strong></p></p><p><strong>Level 2: </strong></p><ul><li><strong>Calling the Aura's Remnant:</strong> Allowing the vampire to speak with a corpse's aura (not their ghost)</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Communicate with Kindred Sire</strong>: Creates a telepathic link between a childe and their sire.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Eyes of Babel</strong>: The caster gains the ability to read and speak any language known by their target.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Illuminate the Trail of Prey</strong>: Allows the caster to perceive the past whereabouts of an individual through a glowing trail.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Ishtar's Touch</strong>: The caster turns a dose of their own vitae into a narcotic, 'truth-serum' like substance that leaves a victim more suggestible and vulnerable to mind-affecting Disciplines like Presence and Dominate.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Truth of Blood</strong>: Creates a potion capable of discerning lies from truth in a statement.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Ward against Spirits</strong></li></ul></details><h2>Domain</h2><p>Chasse (3): See shaded section of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1o25Yh7uYAypQKS81oc6ADpYTF2vuNqlK&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> for permitted hunting ground. Default hunting Difficulty is 4.</p><p>Lien (0): No modifier to interactions with native mortals or for finding/investigating within domain.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p><strong>La Tremere Bibliothèque et Chantry</strong></p><p><em>Le monastère des Augustines de l’Hôpital général de Québec</em></p><p>House Tremere has established a chantry in the closed-off sections of the old monastery. It has a modest library and two shared ritual spaces.</p><h2>Humanity 7</h2><h2>Predator Type: Bagger</h2><h2>Blood Potency 1</h2><p>You have a Bane Severity of 1.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li>Enemy (2): House Goratrix, Sybille Thea</li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Blood Sorcery (3)</h2><p>Type: Sorcery</p><h3>A Taste for Blood</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Blood Sorcery</p><p>Duration: N/A</p><h3>Extinguish Vitae</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Intelligence + Blood Sorcery vs Stamina + Composure</p><p>Duration: N/A</p><h3>Blood of Potency</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Blood Sorcery</p><p>Duration: One scene or one night</p><h2>Dominate (2)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Compel</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Dominate vs Intelligence + Resolve</p><p>Duration: No more than a single scene</p><h3>Mesmerize</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Manipulation + Dominate vs Intelligence + Resolve</p><h2>Rituals</h2><p><strong>Wake with Evening's Freshness (1)</strong>: Allows the caster to freshly awaken from torpor during the day as if it were already evening.</p><p><strong>Ishtar's Touch (2)</strong>: The caster turns a dose of their own vitae into a narcotic, 'truth-serum' like substance that leaves a victim more suggestible and vulnerable to mind-affecting Disciplines like Presence and Dominate.</p><h2>Loresheet: The Pyramid</h2>"},{"slug":"nico","name":"Nico","clan":"Malkavian","faction":"Formerly Sabbat","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","concept":"","bloodPotency":"1","humanity":"6","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/nico.webp","html":"<ul><li class=\"todo\"> Can never remember passwords</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Sensitive about age; appears to be the youngest but is the oldest.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Very good at a musical instrument of your choice (harmonica)</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> You've amassed a very large library as well</li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><blockquote>An absent-minded lech such as yourself may notice that histories, both personal and societal, suffer themes and variations. The Levant harkens, leaving a vacuum to be abhorred à la débandade. Surely an oracle such as yourself sees the opportunity in this. It would please me greatly to consult.<br><br>Yours truly, Baruch</blockquote><h3>Character Notes</h3><p>Old chill, lecherous dude.</p><h3>History</h3><p>1850s; turned in the 1870s.<br>Have them hanging out with various poets and philosophers.</p><p>turned in the 1930s, 1940s.</p><p>Someone turned this guy as the consequence of someone's accident or oversight. regretted or didn't even intend it.</p><h3>Ambition</h3><p>To understand what it means to be 20 in every decade until the end of time.</p><h3>Desire</h3><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><ul><li>Sex is consensual. No lying or using compulsion to get laid. Following that - feed or murder away. It's just not sporting otherwise and an consensual existence is a vital aspect of humanity.<ul><li>Anja, and her descendants</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>There's such a thing as human time.<ul><li>Jake is a 30ish dude who used to be a badass surfer, but has been convinced to become a remote working shut-in. This dude maintains my vamp's vision of time that facilitates a concern for the intersection of those powers that primates w/ digital watches are usually concerned with identifying as casual points. This forcibly retired surfer keeps Nico's \"now\" reasonably enough sized that he can focus on human matters. </li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>The gaze of an(other) defines us.<ul><li>Tristan is an artist who captured an aspect of Nico that he hates---himself lost in time and a bit ravenous. Nico recognizes the value of the sketch and keeps the artist alive despite hating his vision.</li></ul></li></ul><h3>Lore Notes</h3><h2>Domain</h2><p>Chasse (3): See shaded section of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1o25Yh7uYAypQKS81oc6ADpYTF2vuNqlK&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> for permitted hunting ground. Default hunting Difficulty is 4.</p><p>Lien (0): No modifier to interactions with native mortals or for finding/investigating within domain.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p><strong>Comte Cioran's Crypt, Cimetière de l'Hôpital-Général de Québec</strong></p><p>The mausoleum your coterie guarded was for Comte Cioran, an Anarch Brujah who was immensely powerful throughout the twentieth century and ruled Quebec City (and held sway over much of Quebec), keeping independent and holding off all comers, including werewolves, Sabbat, and Camarilla.</p><p>The events leading to his torpor are contradictory, but the guarding of his tomb became a priority for all factions; those who honored his memory wished to prevent a true death or diablerie, and those who feared his return wished to ensure he remained in torpor.</p><p>When he arose, it was with a single-mindedness that led him to the Levant and the rumored location of the Antediluvian founder of the Brujah; leaving the crypt complex a hollow shell.</p><p>Supernature abhors a void, and of late you have been accumulating evidence that this haven now also hosts a wraith or revenant, but you have as yet avoided direct confrontation and have been unable to expel it.</p><h2>Humanity 6</h2><h2>Predator Type: Siren</h2><h2>Blood Potency 1</h2><p>You have a Bane Severity of 1.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><ul><li>Resources: Rich (3)</li></ul><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li class=\"own\">Hopeless Addiction (Alcohol) (2):</li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><p><em>Lost in Space and Time</em>: Upon failing a rouse check, suffer as visual and auditory hallucinations become indistinguishable from reality, until a Composure + Awareness difficulty 3 test succeeds, or until you feed, or until you rest.</p><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Obfuscate (2)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Unseen Passage</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Duration: One scene or until detection.</p><h2>Dominate (1)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Compel</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Dominate vs Intelligence + Resolve</p><p>Duration: No more than a single scene</p><h3>Mesmerize</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Manipulation + Dominate vs Intelligence + Resolve</p><h2>Auspex (1)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Heightened Senses</h3><p>Cost: Free (but see below)</p><p>Dice Pools: Wits + Resolve</p><h2>Loresheet: FIRSTLIGHT</h2><p class=\"own\">Evasion Tactics (1):</p>"},{"slug":"richart-cartier","name":"Richart Cartier","clan":"Tzimisce","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Ancillae (11th Generation)","concept":"Waters of Blatno jezero, aka Lake Balaton","bloodPotency":"2","humanity":"6","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/richart-cartier.webp","html":"<h3>To-Do</h3><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Ambition &amp; Desire</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Maybe he experiments with body parts of his patients? And sells them to help people hide from their enemies?</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> He prefers to wear the hands of people who were on gameshows.<ul><li class=\"todo\"> Vanna White hands</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Self-conscious? Always wears gloves</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Despite his charm, in private he had an offputting habit of chewing 'his' fingernails when nervous, and sometimes cuts a little deeper.</li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><h3>Character Notes</h3><p>Cartier [did something], resulting in his hands being chopped off by his elders.</p><p>His goal is to successfully regrow or shape replacement hands.</p><p>Has since surpassed Milica in status, struck out on his own.</p><p>Currently must sew hands from corpses and vitalize them with vitae. </p><p>Keeps a small bank of hands frozen. Hands are constantly necrotizing.</p><p>Constantly wears gloves atop hands. If they are necrotic they may start to smell, which he covers up with the strong odor of cleaning fluid or cologne.</p><p>Has a large tub filled with the waters of Blatno jezero, aka Lake Balaton, which he must bathe in daily to assuage his clan bane.</p><p>Uses his mouth and tongue to trigger vicissitude. Has a bit of a frog tongue (~5ft range).</p><p>Pushes blood bags through the black market in conjuction with Nosferatu.</p><p>Cartier formally left the Sabbat to live amongst Anarchs between the third and fourth internecine conflict (after 1960).</p><h3>History</h3><p>Embraced by Milica in 1863 along with a few dozen others, and was buried in a mass grave on the Blatno Jezero before he could frenzy. Awoke and fought his way to survive, and was used as cannon fodder in the second Sabbat civil war. As the sole progeny from that conflict to survive, Milica led him through the creation rite and ceremony to recognize him as True Sabbat.</p><h3>Ambition</h3><h3>Desire</h3><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><h3>Lore Notes</h3><details open><summary>Lore Notes on Tzimisce</summary><p>To me a Tzimisce has this one important trait : they're domain owners. Domain is all important to them, as well as all household related etiquette. This may not be the main trait of the character, but it is a vital piece of who they are as Kindred. A bit like certain person who define themselves as \"parents\" (especially as \"mothers\", come on, you know what I'm talking about). In French we have an expression: running a house \"en bon père de famille\" (\"as a good household-father\", in due and proper ways). I can't stress enough the importance of domain, domain-holding, territory and possessiveness the Tzimisce can display. This can be displayed in numerous different ways, but their attachment to something physical such as a haven or their regular servants, as an extension of themselves. Of course they are disposable, like anything else, but surely something interesting can be done there! Be original in those territorial issues, ancesters and the importance of lands, seneschal...</p><p>The new Tzimisce from the Vampire: The Masquerade Companion have gone in a new direction that makes them more relatable and understandable as villains. They still possess the powers of Vicissitude and it's just as potent as it was before, but it's no longer the defining feature of the clan. The new Tzimisce are focused on domination. They are the ultimate control freaks and they are possessive of everything they feel belongs to them. The new Tzimisce are similar to the Ventrue in many respects, though they are a lot harder to reason with. The sadistic scholars of old have been replaced with people with an overwhelming desire for domination. This can take many forms, from noble Lords to corporate executives. A small-time Tzimisce gangster who controls a street corner can be just as possessive about their domain as a duke is with their lands.</p></details><details open><summary>Lore Notes on Sabbat</summary><p>The typical attitude is that being a True Sabbat is a matter of importance and distinction – you do not want just anybody coming in and claiming all the rights and privileges of Sabbat without having proven themselves first. Also, given the pack structure of the sect, many members think of themselves as a collection of gangs or neo-feudal warbands, complete with initiation rites and other ways of making themselves feel special.</p><p>Many neonates in the sect wonder why they have to bother with all these trappings of espionage: is not the Sabbat's mission statement to tear down the Camarilla and its Masquerade and rule humans openly? Sabbat elders who lived through the Inquisition do not dignify these questions with an answer, and even bishops are hard-pressed to come up with a convincing response.</p><p>Although Sabbat vampires may sire childer as usual, and are no less picky than any other vampire about it, during a war effort, they often backdrop to use Mass Embraces for a steady supply of shock troopers. These unfortunate vampires are knocked over, Embraced and buried. By the time the so-called \"shovelhead\" has clawed himself up, he is usually confused and aggressive and then directed with the rest of the Mass Embrace in a first vinculum against the enemy. Most shovelheads do not survive their first weeks, they are considered False Sabbat and are not respected in any way by the members of the sect. Once they have proven themselves repeatedly, they are usually introduced into the sect and undergo the Creation Rites to become True Sabbat. Childer who are specifically chosen to be Embraced often receive this instructions much earlier directly from their sire.</p><p>The cornerstone of Sabbat organization is the pack; Sabbat packs are organizations of 3-10 vampires mutually bound through the standard blood-sharing rites of the cult. Packs have a ductus, who is the pack's warleader, and a pack priest who reminds the pack of its responsibilities to Caine. In addition, pack members are mutually bound in a vinculum – a sort of communal blood bond – created by the blood-sharing ceremonies. Packs generally occupy communal havens; given the Sabbat's rejection of human mores and its use of artificial loyalties enforced by the vinculum, there is less need for privacy.</p></details><h2>Domain</h2><p>Chasse (3): See shaded section of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1o25Yh7uYAypQKS81oc6ADpYTF2vuNqlK&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> for permitted hunting ground. Default hunting Difficulty is 4.</p><p>Lien (0): No modifier to interactions with native mortals or for finding/investigating within domain.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p><strong>Under Hôpital-Général de Québec</strong></p><p>Richart keeps a large haven with a laboratory in a seemingly sealed off tunnel beneath the general hospital. He keeps a selection of hands and other body parts refrigerated by generator power.</p><h2>Humanity 6</h2><h2>Predator Type: Sandman</h2><h2>Blood Potency 2</h2><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/5d8667a60e0e8eaa.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/5d8667a60e0e8eaa.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><ul><li>Haven: Large, with laboratory (4)</li></ul><ul><li>Resources: Rich (3)</li></ul><ul><li>Mask: Presents as a surgeon, with paperwork (1)</li></ul><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li>Tabula Rasa: Does not recall life before Embrace (1)</li></ul><ul><li>Necrotic Hands (2)<ul><li>Upon rousing, you must make an additional rouse check. Failing the rouse check or refusing to perform it causes 1 Superficial damage, or converts a Superficial to Aggravated. If there is already Aggravated damage, the hands must be severed or each subsequent night additional forced damage will be taken. Replacing the hands is a Dexterity + Medicine (3) test.</li></ul></li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Auspex (1)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Sense the Unseen</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Wits + Auspex or Resolve + Auspex</p><p>Duration: Passive</p><h2>Dominate (2)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Cloud Memory</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Dominate vs Wits + Resolve </p><p>Duration: Indefinitely</p><h3>Domitor’s favor</h3><p>Level 2</p><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Duration: One month</p><h2>Loresheet: Sect War Veteran</h2><h3>Trophy Kill</h3><h2>Protean (3)</h2><p>Type: Physical</p><h3>Eyes of the beast</h3><p>Level 1</p><p>Cost: Free</p><p>System: No roll is required to activate Eyes of the Beast.</p><p>Duration: As long as desired</p><h3>Vicissitude</h3><p>Level 2</p><p>Amalgam: Dominate 2</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Protean</p><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>System: Roll Resolve + Protean.</p><p>Duration: Permanent</p><h3>Fleshcrafting</h3><p>Level 3</p><p>Amalgam: Dominate 2</p><p>Prerequisite: Vicissitude</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Protean vs Stamina + Resolve</p><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Duration: Permanent</p>"},{"slug":"kamaludeen-hussein","name":"Kamaludeen Hussein","clan":"Banu Haqim","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","concept":"","bloodPotency":"2","humanity":"5","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/kamaludeen-hussein.webp","html":"<h3>To-Do</h3><ul><li class=\"todo\"> He likes to feed where he knows people are able to watch him.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> He likes feeding on people in casinos.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Arachnophobia</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> He doesn't trust motorized transportation - like no buses, cars, etc.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Maybe he likes to document his feedings, whether with journal entries or photos or video?</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Concept</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Appearance</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> History</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Ambition &amp; Desire</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Sire</li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><blockquote>To our austere Assamite,<br>A Spaniard ductus walks carelessly through these streets. It would be tragic if the steel trap of a kind of justice were to snap upon him, and he be waylaid.<br><br>His blood is old and strong and, while I am no sommelier, carries certain notes that you may be able to appreciate.<br><br>Yours, Baruch Espinosa</blockquote><p>Loyal soldier<br>Interrogator type skill set.<br>Spy</p><h3>Character Notes</h3><h3>History</h3><h3>Ambition</h3><h3>Desire</h3><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><p>The guilty must be punished.<p>Transgressor. Public Figure. TBD.</p></p><h3>Lore Notes</h3><h2>Domain</h2><p>Chasse (3): See shaded section of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1o25Yh7uYAypQKS81oc6ADpYTF2vuNqlK&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> for permitted hunting ground. Default hunting Difficulty is 4.</p><p>Lien (0): No modifier to interactions with native mortals or for finding/investigating within domain.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p><strong>Comte Cioran's Crypt, Cimetière de l'Hôpital-Général de Québec</strong></p><p>The mausoleum your coterie guarded was for Comte Cioran, an Anarch Brujah who was immensely powerful throughout the twentieth century and ruled Quebec City (and held sway over much of Quebec), keeping independent and holding off all comers, including werewolves, Sabbat, and Camarilla.</p><p>The events leading to his torpor are contradictory, but the guarding of his tomb became a priority for all factions; those who honored his memory wished to prevent a true death or diablerie, and those who feared his return wished to ensure he remained in torpor.</p><p>When he arose, it was with a single-mindedness that led him to the Levant and the rumored location of the Antediluvian founder of the Brujah; leaving the crypt complex a hollow shell.</p><p>Supernature abhors a void, and of late you have been accumulating evidence that this haven now also hosts a wraith or revenant, but you have as yet avoided direct confrontation and have been unable to expel it.</p><h2>Humanity 5</h2><h2>Predator Type: Blood Leech</h2><h2>Blood Potency 2</h2><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/355fbd6e566d1a6b.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/355fbd6e566d1a6b.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li>Shunned (2): by whom?</li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Blood Sorcery (3)</h2><p>Type: Sorcery</p><h3>A Taste for Blood</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Blood Sorcery</p><p>Duration: N/A</p><h3>Extinguish Vitae</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Intelligence + Blood Sorcery vs Stamina + Composure</p><p>Duration: N/A</p><h3>Blood of Potency</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Blood Sorcery</p><p>Duration: One scene or one night</p><h2>Obfuscate (1)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Silence of Death</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Duration: One scene</p><h2>Protean (1)</h2><p>Type: Physical</p><h3>Eyes of the Beast</h3><p>Level 1</p><p>Cost: Free</p><p>System: No roll is required to activate Eyes of the Beast.</p><p>Duration: As long as desired</p><h2>Rituals</h2><p><strong>Blood Walk</strong>: An advanced version of <strong>A Taste for Blood</strong>, the caster is able to learn even more information about another Kindred from their vitae.</p><p><strong>Ishtar's Touch</strong>: The caster turns a dose of their own vitae into a narcotic, 'truth-serum' like substance that leaves a victim more suggestible and vulnerable to mind-affecting Disciplines like Presence and Dominate.</p><p>Ingredients: A gold inlaid ceremonial dagger</p>"},{"slug":"susanna","name":"Susanna","clan":"Salubri","faction":"Unaffiliated","generation":"Ancillae (10th Generation)","concept":"Slouching towards Golconda","bloodPotency":"4","humanity":"7","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/susanna.webp","html":"<h3>To-Do</h3><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Ambition &amp; Desire</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Convictions (1-3)</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Touchstones (1-3)</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Traits</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Skills</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo done\"> Actually knowing the body of animals</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Very particular about blood temperature when feeding.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo done\"> Susanna uses secret ingredients in her meals that she may or may not have purchased items from Richart?</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Or only feeds on vegans?</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo done\"> Still feeling very empathetic; uses her knowledge of anatomy to feed in </li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><h3>Character Notes</h3><p>Susanna has a famulus, a dog named Sunshine.</p><h3>History</h3><p>Former chef before being embraced by Estelle.</p><h3>Ambition</h3><h3>Desire</h3><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><ul><li>No harm to animals<ul><li>Sunshine the dog, is a bond famulus</li></ul></li></ul><h3>Lore Notes</h3><h2>Humanity 7</h2><h2>Predator Type: Osiris</h2><h2>Blood Potency 4</h2><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/3523c12f89a12cfd.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/3523c12f89a12cfd.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><ul><li>Fame (3)</li></ul><ul><li>Satisfy the Hunger (4, see Golconda)</li></ul><ul><li>Greet the Sun (5, see Golconda)</li></ul><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li>Known Blankbody (2)</li></ul><ul><li>Compromised Haven (2)</li></ul><ul><li>Enemies: Tremere (2)</li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Auspex</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Sense the Unseen</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Wits + Auspex or Resolve + Auspex</p><p>Duration: Passive</p><h3>Premonition</h3><p>Cost: Free or one Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Auspex</p><p>Duration: Passive</p><h3>Scry the Soul</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Intelligence + Auspex vs Composure + Subterfuge</p><p>Duration: One turn, or Storyteller’s discretion</p><h3>Share the Senses</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Resolve + Auspex</p><p>Duration: One scene</p><h2>Dominate</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Cloud Memory</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Dominate vs Wits + Resolve </p><p>Duration: Indefinitely</p><h2>Animalism</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><p>Blood Resonance: Animal blood, preferably feral.</p><h3>Bond Famulus</h3><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Animal Ken</p><h2>Loresheet: Golconda</h2><ul><li class=\"own\">Satisfy the Hunger:</li></ul><figure>https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/secure.notion-static.com/af9d7a25-fdcb-4667-8640-645fde7e2101/Salubri.pdf</figure>"},{"slug":"calliope","name":"Calliope","clan":"Brujah","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Fledgling (13th Generation)","concept":"","bloodPotency":"1","humanity":"6","portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/calliope.webp","html":"<h3>To-Do</h3><ul><li class=\"todo done\"> Ambition &amp; Desire</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Fast walker, keep up and get out of my way.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> Superstitious about walking under ladders, etc.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> She is rumored to have massacred a gang for interrupting a smoke with an initiation.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"todo\"> I wasn't hungry, but you were upsetting me.</li></ul><h3>Session Notes</h3><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/caf637c07e819dca.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/caf637c07e819dca.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><p>Claire wants to rebuild clan Tremere/Cam and is focused on restoring her clan. </p><ul><li>Maybe Calliope helps her even though it's a different clan?</li></ul><ul><li>Callie's love of community supersedes the separation of the clans?</li></ul><ul><li>Baroch doesn't care who is in power so long as I help seize it?</li></ul><h3>Character Notes</h3><ul><li>abandoned by mother and has strong connections to her father.<ul><li>Father was someone important in the city. </li></ul><ul><li>He is responsible for building many of the educational institutions and safe havens (orphanages, libraries, schools, hospitals)</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>Callie was raised with strong faith and strong bonds to the church.<ul><li>People have twisted the teachings to fit their own agenda.</li></ul><ul><li>Churches have become money hungry and began excluding populations of people marking them as weak or less-than.</li></ul><ul><li>In an attempt to find her own way and unite others something happened and she was turned?</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>Quick tempered. Fast walker and talker.</li></ul><ul><li>Superstitious.</li></ul><ul><li>Possible rumor - she once massacred a gang for interrupting an initiation. We don't know if it's true or not.</li></ul><ul><li>Connected to Jerome \"The Bank\" and the pack of Gangrel.</li></ul><h3>History</h3><p>Anarch</p><h3>Ambition</h3><p>To restore the churches in the city to the feeling of real community and safe haven (as opposed to the corruption they are under today). </p><p>Maybe vampires and humans?</p><h3>Desire</h3><p>To find Elua and see if he is OK.</p><h3>Convictions &amp; Touchstones</h3><p>T: Callie's father who built many of the libraries in the city as a promise to her that she would always have a place of solace after her mother abandoned them.</p><p>C: Always keep your sworn word.</p><p>T: Preacher Elua, who always taught her to value the lives of others.</p><p>C: Protect the innocent.</p><h3>Lore Notes</h3><h2>Domain</h2><p>Chasse (3): See shaded section of <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1o25Yh7uYAypQKS81oc6ADpYTF2vuNqlK&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> for permitted hunting ground. Default hunting Difficulty is 4.</p><p>Lien (0): No modifier to interactions with native mortals or for finding/investigating within domain.</p><h2>Haven</h2><p><strong>Comte Cioran's Crypt, Cimetière de l'Hôpital-Général de Québec</strong></p><p>The mausoleum your coterie guarded was for Comte Cioran, an Anarch Brujah who was immensely powerful throughout the twentieth century and ruled Quebec City (and held sway over much of Quebec), keeping independent and holding off all comers, including werewolves, Sabbat, and Camarilla.</p><p>The events leading to his torpor are contradictory, but the guarding of his tomb became a priority for all factions; those who honored his memory wished to prevent a true death or diablerie, and those who feared his return wished to ensure he remained in torpor.</p><p>When he arose, it was with a single-mindedness that led him to the Levant and the rumored location of the Antediluvian founder of the Brujah; leaving the crypt complex a hollow shell.</p><p>Supernature abhors a void, and of late you have been accumulating evidence that this haven now also hosts a wraith or revenant, but you have as yet avoided direct confrontation and have been unable to expel it.</p><h2>Humanity 6</h2><h2>Predator Type: Alleycat</h2><h2>Blood Potency 1</h2><p>You have a Bane Severity of 1.</p><figure><a href=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"campaign/assets/pages/b432381782817113.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></figure><h2>Blush of Life</h2><h2>Blood Surge</h2><h2>Vampiric Mending</h2><p><em>Mending superficial health damage</em></p><p><em>Mending aggravated health damage</em></p><h1>Advantages</h1><h2>Merits</h2><ul><li>Criminal Contacts (3)</li></ul><h2>Flaws</h2><ul><li class=\"own\">- refuse to hunt/feed on women.</li></ul><ul><li class=\"own\">Suspect (Camarilla) You’re not good with this sect at all.</li></ul><h2>Clan Bane</h2><h2>Clan Compulsion</h2><h1>Disciplines</h1><h2>Potence (3)</h2><p>Type: Physical</p><h3>Lethal Body</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Duration: Passive</p><h3>Prowess</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Duration: One scene</p><h3>Spark of Rage</h3><p>Amalgam: Presence 3</p><p>Cost: One Rouse Check </p><p>Dice Pools: Manipulation + Potence</p><p>Duration: One Scene</p><h2>Presence (3)</h2><p>Type: Mental</p><h3>Awe</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Dice Pools: Manipulation + Presence vs Composure + Intelligence</p><p>Duration: One scene or until intentionally ended</p><h3>Daunt</h3><p>Cost: Free</p><p>Duration: One scene or until intentionally ended</p><h3>Dread Gaze</h3><p>Cost: One Rouse Check</p><p>Dice Pools: Charisma + Presence vs Composure + Resolve</p><p>Duration: One turn</p>"}],"personae":[{"slug":"estelle-de-leon","name":"Estelle De León","title":"","clan":"Salubri","faction":"Unaffiliated","generation":"Elder (9th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-11th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/estelle-de-leon.webp"},{"slug":"milica-zupancic","name":"Milica Zupančič","title":"Bishop","clan":"Tzimisce","faction":"Sabbat","generation":"Ancillae (10th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/milica-zupancic.webp"},{"slug":"jerome-the-bank-giovanni","name":"Jerome “The Bank” Giovanni","title":"","clan":"Hecata","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021","epilogue"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/jerome-the-bank-giovanni.webp"},{"slug":"prince-beatrice-bouchard","name":"Prince Beatrice Bouchard","title":"Prince of Quebec City","clan":"Ventrue","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Ancillae (10th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/prince-beatrice-bouchard.webp"},{"slug":"gisele-singh","name":"Gisele Singh","title":"Seneschal","clan":"Ventrue","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/gisele-singh.webp"},{"slug":"javier-pegahmagabow","name":"Javier Pegahmagabow","title":"Sheriff","clan":"Banu Haqim","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-11th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/javier-pegahmagabow.webp"},{"slug":"anselm","name":"Anselm","title":"Harpy","clan":"Nosferatu","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-12th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/anselm.webp"},{"slug":"michel-delacroix","name":"Michel Delacroix","title":"Tremere Primogen","clan":"Tremere","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021","epilogue"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/michel-delacroix.webp"},{"slug":"maggie-molyneux","name":"Maggie Molyneux","title":"Toreador Primogen","clan":"Toreador","faction":"Camarilla","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-12th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/maggie-molyneux.webp"},{"slug":"the-spaniard","name":"“The Spaniard”","title":"Ductus","clan":"Lasombra","faction":"Sabbat","generation":"Neonate (12th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-9th-2021","night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-11th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021","epilogue"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/the-spaniard.webp"},{"slug":"faith","name":"Faith","title":"","clan":"The Ministry","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/faith.webp"},{"slug":"councillor-rene-lefebvre","name":"Councillor Rene Lefebvre","title":"Councillor","clan":"","faction":"Society of St. Leopold","generation":"","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/councillor-rene-lefebvre.webp"},{"slug":"glaurung","name":"Glaurung","title":"Bishop","clan":"Tzimisce","faction":"Sabbat","generation":"Ancillae (10th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/glaurung.webp"},{"slug":"jonah-weber","name":"Jonah Weber","title":"","clan":"Caitiff","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Thin-Blood (15th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/jonah-weber.webp"},{"slug":"linh-phuong","name":"Linh Phuong","title":"","clan":"Caitiff","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Thin-Blood (16th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/linh-phuong.webp"},{"slug":"matthieu-dufourmantelle","name":"Matthieu Dufourmantelle","title":"","clan":"Gangrel","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/matthieu-dufourmantelle.webp"},{"slug":"roscoe","name":"Roscoe","title":"","clan":"Brujah","faction":"Sabbat","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/roscoe.webp"},{"slug":"stefan-neptune","name":"Stefan Neptune","title":"","clan":"The Ministry","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Neonate (13th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/stefan-neptune.webp"},{"slug":"sybille-thea","name":"Sybille Théa","title":"Ductus","clan":"Tremere","faction":"Sabbat","generation":"Ancillae (11th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/sybille-thea.webp"},{"slug":"comte-cioran","name":"Comte Cioran","title":"Comte","clan":"Brujah","faction":"Anarch","generation":"Elder (8th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-11th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/comte-cioran.webp"},{"slug":"baruch-espinosa","name":"Baruch Espinosa","title":"","clan":"Nosferatu","faction":"Unaffiliated","generation":"Ancillae (11th Generation)","nights":["night-of-june-9th-2021","night-of-june-10th-2021","night-of-june-11th-2021","night-of-june-12th-2021","night-of-june-13th-2021","night-of-june-14th-2021"],"portrait":"campaign/assets/portraits/baruch-espinosa.webp"}]};
